@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# Specialty Directory Assembled In Memory From Two Reads
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The specialty directory reads the veterinarian–specialty relationship from the specialty side. `Vet` maps that relationship in one direction only, through a join table. `Specialty` holds no reference back.
+
+The page must list every specialty the clinic knows, including one that no veterinarian holds. Neither existing repository can answer that. `VetRepository` reaches specialties only through veterinarians, so an unheld specialty is unreachable.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Inverse association on `Specialty`** — add a mapped-by collection of veterinarians to the entity, and read the directory from it.
+2. **Join query** — add a repository query returning specialty-and-veterinarian pairs with an outer join, and group the rows.
+3. **Two reads, assembled in memory** — list the specialties from a new repository, list the veterinarians from the existing one, and pair them in an immutable projection.
+
+## Decision
+
+Option 3. `SpecialtyRepository` returns every specialty in name order. `VetRepository.findAll()` returns the veterinarians with their specialties already fetched. `SpecialtyDirectory` pairs them.
+
+Option 1 makes a shared entity bidirectional. The cycle it creates reaches the serialized veterinarian route, which is a known defect pending removal. Option 2 adds query machinery for a result the two existing reads already contain.
+
+Option 3 leaves `Specialty` untouched, reuses the cached veterinarian read, and places the pairing in a type that runs without MVC infrastructure. The `Web controller` row of [architecture-principles.md](../architecture-principles.md#in-force) admits no rule into the controller, so the pairing needs a home outside it.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Both tables are read in full on every request. The directory carries no paging requirement and the seeded data is a handful of rows.
+- The directory inherits the `vets` cache, which has no eviction configured. Stale veterinarian data reaches this page exactly as it reaches the veterinarian directory.
+- `SpecialtyDirectory` is a value object, testable with real `Vet` and `Specialty` instances and no Spring context.
+- A clinic large enough to make the full read costly needs option 2. The change is confined to the repository and the projection's factory.
+- `Specialty` gains no collection, so the serialized veterinarian route is unaffected.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the three contracts this decision introduces
+- [2026-07-31-relational-persistence-with-spring-data-jpa.md](2026-07-31-relational-persistence-with-spring-data-jpa.md) — the repository and mapping style this follows
+- [2026-07-31-feature-package-organization.md](2026-07-31-feature-package-organization.md) — why the new types sit in the `vet` package
